--------------------------- Changelog -----------------------------

1.0.d - UNRELEASED
Changed - The Stigmata-class Harpoon Tug and the Reliquary-class LYNE Tender have their own hulls and stats: the Stigmata a fast midline destroyer with a fighter bay and a built-in harpoon mount, the Reliquary a slow midline carrier cruiser with two fighter bays, meant for two built-in wings of LYNE drones. Their combat equipment comes later
Fixed - Fleets already offering a quest, or whose commander is marked important for a mission, no longer take on a fishing job as well
Changed - The marker beside a fleet whose fishing job you have accepted is now a steady gold instead of pulsing; offers still pulse light blue
Changed - Codex entries known only from range data show no fish icon, in the list or on their page, until you catch the fish
Fixed - A fish's codex list icon no longer stays blank until its art has been shown elsewhere, such as on its codex page
Fixed - Restless fish such as the Flarefin Koi no longer circle almost in place when Breach Lights surface or slow them; their weave narrows with their pace
Changed - The Retrieval Head and Fanned Array are no longer sold or given as rewards. They will come with the fishing ships, which add a second equipment slot to their rig while they are in your fleet. Copies you already own are kept
Added - Reployment Bays, a Drone Core module that comes with the Reliquary-class LYNE Tender: whenever every drone has come back, the whole swarm goes out again until you recall it or it can no longer fish where you are
Added - After the tutorial, the Fisherman has a treasure rumour for a nearby system in place of the free lead, and shows the system on the map as he offers it. He has lost a golden chest there: it can come up in the catch window on lamp catches in that system (30% each, and certain on the 4th, then every 2nd, until taken). Bring back the compass inside for the Glitter Lens schematic plus the fish and credits to buy it; an intel entry tracks buying it, the lens goes on your Outfitter shopping list, and his Outfitter option is highlighted until you buy it
Added - If you lose the Fisherman's compass, tell him: he remembers where it was sold, checks your storage, and if it is gone for good he pays you anyway
Changed - The treasure rumour's bycatch boost lasts until you return the compass, then another two months once you buy the Glitter Lens
Added - Once the Glitter Lens is built, the Fisherman passes on a request from an old crewman: a captain hunting an epic in a nearby system with no markets, whose Breach Lights have failed; the system shows on the map as he asks. His fleet carries the fishing-job marker, light blue until you have met him and yellow after, never takes on a fishing job of its own, and once met stays on the map. Keep your lights on within 6,000 units of the star's surface for 15 seconds without a break to find the epic, then harpoon it. Either way he gives you a Stigmata-class Harpoon Tug, with its second Harpoon slot and the Retrieval Head; landing the epic also pays a harpoon module schematic and three range-data entries
Added - Report back to the Fisherman afterwards for a word on hunting epics and the Needle Sensor schematic. An intel entry tracks building it, the sensor goes on your Outfitter shopping list, and his Outfitter option is highlighted until you buy it
Added - With the Needle Sensor built, the Fisherman sends you after a wounded epic circling a planet about 1,000 units out in a nearby empty system, never the captain's system or species; the planet shows on the map as he offers it. Its Needle Sensor ripples trace its circle. It swims at half speed once woken and is the only one of its species in that system while you hunt it. A hunt that loses it, or putting your Breach Lights out while it is awake, sends it back to the planet. Landing it pays the blueprint for the Monstrance-class Breach Trawler, which brings a second Lens Array slot and the Fanned Array, plus range data on an epic. Have the ship built and show him for a last word
Added - After the Monstrance, the Fisherman tells you to improve your gear and listen for rumours. Landing your first legendary completes it, and he hands over a Reliquary-class LYNE Tender, with a second Drone Core slot and the Reployment Bays. From then on a "Hunting the legendary fish" intel lists every legendary: question marks until you hear of one, the name its teller used after that, and its real name once caught
Changed - Legendary rumour intel shows the name the teller used. The bar spacer's stories that name nothing go by a name from the story until you catch the fish
Added - "Surfaced lamp-fish speed (%)" setting in Ruptures & Exploration: the speed of fish that surface in your Breach Lights, as a percentage of their normal speed (100% by default). Lower it to make them easier to chase down
Changed - Ordinary fish now surface as soon as your Breach Lights reach them and swim in their own style until caught or gone; epic and legendary fish still stay hidden until harpooned. Turn this off with "Surface fish in breach lights" in the Ruptures & Exploration settings, or turn on "Straight lamp-fish movement" to have surfaced fish swim the old straight course with a gentle weave instead of their own style
Changed - The Tracking Gimbal also follows fish your Breach Lights have surfaced, and the tracking upgrade keeps them visible and in reach after the beam moves on
Changed - Fight Night's fee option now reads "Take the rewards." and lists the rewards in its tooltip
Changed - Every equipment module costs one price tier more (25,000 to 45,000 credits), and none can be paid for with common fish alone
Added - Glitter Lens, a Lens Array module that doubles the chance of bycatch on catches made under Breach Lights. Its schematic comes only from the Fisherman's treasure rumour, never from job or distress rewards
Changed - The Neutrino Lens only shows its spikes while the Breach Lights are on as well as the Neutrino Detector
Removed - The Breach Coupler is withdrawn for now: it is no longer sold or awarded, and one already fitted does nothing; ROD drones fish ruptures only
Changed - Every epic fish now comes up only under Breach Lights; ruptures fished with the ROD no longer hold them
Changed - Epic fish are now hunted in two stages: they drift slowly until a harpoon hit inside a lit Breach Light beam wakes them, then raise a one-charge shield that never comes back and swim more erratically, staying in view with your lights off; one that gets more than 3,000 units away drifts off and fades, with a notice that it was lost, and an awake epic is gone once you leave the system. Only the harpoon lands one: ROD drones leave epics alone
Added - Version Checker support: update notices, plus the changelog and direct download for LunaLib's update screen and mod managers such as triOS

Development
Adjusted - AddFish accepts a fish ID or full name, followed by quantity, quality and coherence; quantity defaults to 1 and names autocomplete

1.0.c

Quests and payments
Fixed - A camp fleet that loses a fight to you gives up the rupture and leaves, instead of holding it until destroyed
Fixed - Job intel names the market and star system to deliver to, and switches to "Return to" once you have the catch; a cleared camp job points back to the fisher once the proof is aboard
Fixed - Automatic job and Outfitter payments no longer consume legendary fish.
Removed - Disabled legendary tribute at Kanta's Den pending dialogue replacement.

Fleet interactions
Changed - Contract hunters respond less often to single harpoon hits, but may pursue unpaid repair bills or fleeing after identification following a dark hit. Paying the fine calls them off.
Changed - Crews with unpaid repair bills now report you to local patrols instead of chasing you. All patrols in the system demand payment on sight until the fine is paid.

Crablobab
Added - Crablobab sells Party Horn after acquiring Celebration Charges, followed by Crab Fanfare. Both replace the catch sound and can be previewed before purchase and selected in the Outfitter.

Equipment
Added - Neutrino Lens module for the Lens Array. Shows rare, epic and legendary patterns as rarity-coloured Neutrino Detector spikes. Grants the detector if missing.
Fixed - Needle Sensor ripples are larger, brighter and visible at greater zoom distances.

Treasure
Added - Uncommon fishing chests have a 25% chance to contain unknown range data alongside normal loot, including with the Lifting Rig.
Changed - Recovered treasure now has aligned quantities; range data displays as "Range data: <fish>".

Harpoon
Adjusted - Harpoons hitting shields no longer play the catch sound.

Legendaries
Removed - Failed Quorum catches no longer spawn 12 extra decoys.
Fixed - Dormant epics and legendaries now leave trails under breach lights.
Fixed - Loading saves with Lantern Jack surfaced in the current system no longer crashes.
Fixed - Reduced performance cost of epic and legendary trails under breach lights.
Fixed - Legendary floating text use shield or mote colour instead of a generic UI highlight
Added - Lantern Jack now coils for 0.3 seconds within 300 units of a mote, then dashes through it to feed (also: added vfx)

Aquarium
Fixed - Corrected aquarium swimming orientation for 13 species, including Dopefish and several legendaries.

1.0.b

General
Added - Temporary industry image

Fisherman
Fixed - Nearby settlements no longer prevent the Fisherman from approaching you for the tutorial
Fixed - Finishing the Fisherman's "Why a fish?" questions no longer shows an empty Continue before "You could have told me this before I started."
Fixed - Fisherman tutorial lessons no longer send you to systems with a neutron star
Adjusted - The Fisherman's first lesson now points at the rupture closest to him
Added - Selling fish to the Fisherman can unpack crates again after using "Pack into crates"
Fixed - Hovering the "Pack into crates" button in the Fisherman sale screen no longer repeats the click sound
Fixed - Undo in the Fisherman's range data shop takes back every purchase in sequence, newest first, like the Outfitter
Adjusted - Buncha dialogue
Fixed - "Set autopilot" on tutorial and chart request intel now targets a visiting Fisherman in your current system instead of a boat elsewhere

Fish
Added - New portraits for 16 fish that had placeholders until now
Added - Dopefish, a rare Epic catch that barely moves and is very easy to land
Fixed - System fish counts no longer include a species that never spawns there, which made a full system show 16 species
Fixed - A star system never offers more than 15 species; a legendary in a full system temporarily takes one of those slots

Legendaries
Added - Lantern Jack's lure call now plays a distress-call sound
Added - Harpoons deflected by a legendary's shield play a varied shield-hit sound
Added - Epic fish leave a fainter purple version of the legendary trail under breach lights
Adjusted - Buried and diving legendaries and epics no longer leave a trail
Added - A foghorn sounds when a legendary haunt starts and ends

Outfitter
Added - Hovering an Outfitter fish count shows the species of that rarity aboard

Cargo and items
Fixed - Fish, crate and pile tooltips only show their right-click hints for fish in your fleet's cargo, not in markets, storage or selection screens
Adjusted - Fish art on crate labels in cargo is drawn sharper
Adjusted - Tooltips across most items
Fixed - Fish, crates and piles sold to a market now disappear when its stock refreshes

Codex
Added - Codex pages of caught fish show a size distribution chart with your best and latest catch

1.0.a
Added - Initial Mod Release

General
Adjusted - Release downloads leave out development tools, libraries and source files
Adjusted - Rewrote fishing settings descriptions to explain their effects and limits more clearly

Development
Added - Changelog and release instructions
